FileChecksum: SHA256: 7b8ac0f944b7dcbc7df4eb41846135b65e7fe7019ede760c603d5159352b4730
FileChecksum: MD5: 65563b0a4e9ef702dd87a320647971ad
LicenseConcluded: LicenseRef-BSD-2-Clause-2c6f31beafbcf8c8f9095b83d8c5688d AND LicenseRef-BSD-3-Clause-8d8b0539fa1d605c3e5ed913c31623a9
LicenseComments: <text> Addtionally to the text of the BSD-3-Clause license there is the following information in the file:
@license http://www.opensource.org/licenses/bsd-license.php New BSD License
@version CVS: $Id: CSS.php,v 1.89 2009/07/03 15:52:22 farell Exp $
@link http://pear.php.net/package/HTML_CSS
The term New BSD license is associated with the BSD-3-Clause license and not with the BSD-2-Clasue license. We also checked the given link https://pear.php.net/package/HTML_CSS the license information on the page lists BSD with a link. When clicking on the link the text of the BSD-2-Clause license is displayed https://opensource.org/license/BSD-2-Clause thus we concluded additionally BSD-2-Clause as license of this file, with the text displayed on the OSI website
The information was retreived on 27 of Aug 2026
The information in the file is:
@license http://www.opensource.org/licenses/bsd-license.php New BSD License
The link points to the BSD-2-Clause license, but the name New BSD License refers to the BSD-3-Clause license. We concluded here BSD-3-Clause as license of this file, because the name is explicitly mentioned and internet links are volatile. We took the license text from https://opensource.org/license/bsd-3-clause
There is a small risk that this is not the correct license text
The information was retreived on 26th of Aug 2026 </text>
LicenseInfoInFile: LicenseRef-BSD-3-Clause
